              },
              "block": [
                {
                  "text": "Marcel’s mouth opens. “What? Are the men going to steal Zaza Dupont’s diamond?” He remembers an evening at the opera two weeks before. Zaza’s green dress. The music. The beautiful White Star on her finger. “No! They can’t steal it!,” he says. The train comes and the men get on. Marcel pulls down his hat and follows them."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
